        "original_id": "07725cb4-3936-5910-8a7f-030d87c97267",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Cymbidium, Patrinia\n- Places: Sessa Orchid Sanctuary, China, Siberia, Japan\n- Concepts: Orchidaceae, orchid species, Cymbidium hybrids, cut-flower production\n\nFacts:\n- Cymbidium, also called boat orchid, is a genus of 52 evergreen species in the orchid family Orchidaceae.\n- Patrinia has about 17 species native to grassy mountain habitats in China, Siberia, and Japan.\n- Sessa Orchid Sanctuary has a nursery with representative specimens of various orchid species from the sanctuary.\n- Sessa Orchid Sanctuary has a demonstration farm of Cymbidium hybrids for cut-flower production.",
